 implicit `Sized` bound as this is incompatible with [trait object]s"},{"DocComment":" where, by definition, the trait needs to work with all possible implementors,"},{"DocComment":" and thus could be any size."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Although Rust will let you bind `Sized` to a trait, you won't"},{"DocComment":" be able to use it to form a trait object later:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" # #![allow(unused_variables)]"},{"DocComment":" trait Foo { }"},{"DocComment":" trait Bar: Sized { }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" struct Impl;"},{"DocComment":" impl Foo for Impl { }"},{"DocComment":" impl Bar for Impl { }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let x: &dyn Foo = &Impl;    // OK"},{"DocComment":" // let y: &dyn Bar = &Impl; // error: the trait `Bar` cannot be made into an object"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [trait object]: ../../book/ch17-02-trait-objects.html"},{"Builtin":"Fundamental"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":"Sized","diagnostic_item":null},"src":"Normal","generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self","variance":"Unknown"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"implied_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":10,"beg":{"line":158,"col":17},"end":{"line":158,"col":26}},"generated_from_span":null}},"origin":"WhereClauseOnTrait","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[1,0]}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}],"consts":[],"types":[],"methods":[],"vtable":null},{"def_id":1,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["marker",0]},{"Ident":["MetaSized",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":10,"beg":{"line":175,"col":0},"end":{"line":175,"col":33}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Types with a size that can be determined from pointer metadata."},{"Builtin":"Fundamental"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":"MetaSized","diagnostic_item":null},"src":"Normal","generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self","variance":"Unknown"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"implied_clauses":[],"consts":[],"types":[],"methods":[],"vtable":{"id":7,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}},{"def_id":2,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["alloc",0]},{"Ident":["Allocator",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":12,"beg":{"line":201,"col":0},"end":{"line":201,"col":32}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" An implementation of `Allocator` can allocate, grow, shrink, and deallocate arbitrary blocks of"},{"DocComment":" data described via [`Layout`][]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `Allocator` is mostly designed to be implemented on ZSTs, references, or smart pointers,"},{"DocComment":" but can also be implemented directly on the underlying memory-owning type so long as it"},{"DocComment":" upholds the necessary guarantees. In general, an allocator of the type `MyAlloc([u8; N])`"},{"DocComment":" cannot be soundly created without being pinned or otherwise immovable in order to be"},{"DocComment":" correct."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" In contrast to [`GlobalAlloc`][], `Allocator` allows zero-sized allocations. If an underlying"},{"DocComment":" allocator does not support this (like jemalloc) or responds by returning a null pointer"},{"DocComment":" (such as `libc::malloc`), this must be caught by the implementation."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" In order to be usable in a flexible manner while still being sound, implementors of the trait"},{"DocComment":" must uphold very detailed semantics as explained below; the following terms are thus provided"},{"DocComment":" as vocabulary for allocator safety and implementation requirements:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ### Equivalent allocators"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Multiple allocator values can sometimes be interchangeable with each other."},{"DocComment":" When this is the case, we refer to those allocators as being *equivalent* to"},{"DocComment":" each other."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Users of allocators may assume the following are true of equivalent allocators,"},{"DocComment":" and implementors must ensure these rules are upheld:"},{"DocComment":" * An allocator is equivalent to itself. (Equivalence is reflexive.)"},{"DocComment":" * If an allocator is equivalent to a second allocator, then"},{"DocComment":"   the second allocator is also equivalent to the first. (Equivalence is symmetric.)"},{"DocComment":" * If an allocator is equivalent to a second allocator, and"},{"DocComment":"   the second allocator is equivalent to a third allocator, then"},{"DocComment":"   the first allocator is also equivalent to the third allocator."},{"DocComment":"   (Equivalence is transitive.)"},{"DocComment":" * Moving, subtyping, unsize-coercing, or trait-upcasting an allocator does not change"},{"DocComment":"   what the allocator is equivalent to."},{"DocComment":" * Copying or cloning an allocator creates an equivalent one, should the"},{"DocComment":"   [`AllocatorClone`] trait be implemented."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Additionally, implementors of `Allocator` may specify additional equivalences"},{"DocComment":" between allocators. It is the responsibility of such implementors to make sure"},{"DocComment":" that equivalent allocators have \"compatible\" `Allocator` implementations."},{"DocComment":" In particular, the standard library specifies the following equivalences:"},{"DocComment":" * A reference to an allocator (either `&` or `&mut`) is equivalent to"},{"DocComment":"   the allocator being referenced."},{"DocComment":" * A `Box`, `Rc`, or `Arc` containing an allocator is equivalent to"},{"DocComment":"   the allocator inside."},{"DocComment":" * All `Global` allocator instances are equivalent with each other."},{"DocComment":" * All `System` allocator instances are equivalent with each other."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ### Currently allocated memory"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Some of the methods require that a memory block is *currently allocated* by some specific allocator."},{"DocComment":" This means that:"},{"DocComment":" * the starting address for that memory block was previously returned by"},{"DocComment":"   the [`allocate`], [`allocate_zeroed`], [`grow`], [`grow_zeroed`], or [`shrink`] methods,"},{"DocComment":"   called on an allocator that's equivalent to this specific allocator; and"},{"DocComment":" * the memory block has not subsequently been [*invalidated*]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ### Invalidating memory blocks"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" A memory block that is currently allocated becomes *invalidated* when one"},{"DocComment":" of the following happens:"},{"DocComment":" * The memory block is deallocated. This occurs when the memory block"},{"DocComment":"   is passed as an argument to a [`deallocate`] call, or when it is passed"},{"DocComment":"   as an argument to a [`grow`], [`grow_zeroed`] or [`shrink`] call that returns `Ok`."},{"DocComment":" * For all (equivalent) allocators that this memory block is currently allocated by, at"},{"DocComment":"   least one of the following has occurred:"},{"DocComment":"   * The allocator's destructor runs."},{"DocComment":"   * The allocator is mutated through a public or otherwise untrusted API taking `&mut` access."},{"DocComment":"   * One of the borrow-checker lifetimes in the allocator's type expires."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Note that these conditions imply that a collection may ensure that"},{"DocComment":" any specific currently allocated memory block won't be invalidated by:"},{"DocComment":" * not deallocating that memory block,"},{"DocComment":" * owning an allocator that memory block is allocated with, and"},{"DocComment":" * not publicly exposing `&mut` access to that allocator."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Also note that safe public API of an allocator with `&` access is not"},{"DocComment":" allowed to invalidate its memory blocks. Furthermore, unsafe public API"},{"DocComment":" of an allocator with `&` access must document that they invalidate"},{"DocComment":" memory blocks (e.g., by calling `deallocate`) if they do. Therefore,"},{"DocComment":" a collection may safely expose `&` access to its allocator."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Also note that, even in cases where there are other \"alive\" allocators known"},{"DocComment":" to be equivalent to a given collection's allocator, most collections still should"},{"DocComment":" not publicly expose `&mut` access to their allocators. The fact that there are"},{"DocComment":" other \"alive\" allocators would prevent this `&mut` access from invalidating"},{"DocComment":" the collection's memory block, but public `&mut` access is still likely to"},{"DocComment":" be unsound, since a user could replace the collection's allocator with"},{"DocComment":" a non-equivalent allocator, causing the collection to deallocate its memory"},{"DocComment":" with the wrong allocator."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`allocate`]: Allocator::allocate"},{"DocComment":" [`allocate_zeroed`]: Allocator::allocate_zeroed"},{"DocComment":" [`grow`]: Allocator::grow"},{"DocComment":" [`grow_zeroed`]: Allocator::grow_zeroed"},{"DocComment":" [`shrink`]: Allocator::shrink"},{"DocComment":" [`deallocate`]: Allocator::deallocate"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ### Memory fitting"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Some of the methods require that a `layout` *fits* a memory block or vice versa. This means"},{"DocComment":" that the following conditions must hold:"},{"DocComment":"  * the memory block must be *currently allocated* with alignment of [`layout.align()`], and"},{"DocComment":"  * [`layout.size()`] must fall in the range `min ..= max`, where:"},{"DocComment":"    - `min` is the size of the layout used to allocate the block, and"},{"DocComment":"    - `max` is the actual size returned from [`allocate`], [`allocate_zeroed`],"},{"DocComment":"      [`grow`], [`grow_zeroed`], or [`shrink`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`layout.align()`]: Layout::align"},{"DocComment":" [`layout.size()`]: Layout::size"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Safety"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Implementors of `Allocator` must ensure that a memory block that"},{"DocComment":" is [*currently allocated*] by the allocator points to valid memory"},{"DocComment":" until that memory block is [*invalidated*]. The implementor must also"},{"DocComment":" not violate this invariant of `Allocator` via allocator equivalences"},{"DocComment":" that are in the implementor's control."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Additionally, any memory block returned by the allocator must"},{"DocComment":" satisfy the allocation invariants described in `core::ptr`."},{"DocComment":" In particular, if a block has base address `p` and size `n`,"},{"DocComment":" then `p as usize + n <= usize::MAX` must hold. These blocks must also"},{"DocComment":" be wholly disjoint."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This ensures that pointer arithmetic within the allocation"},{"DocComment":" (for example, `ptr.add(len)`) cannot overflow the address space, and"},{"DocComment":" that it is possible to perform nonoverlapping copies between allocations."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" None of the allocating or deallocating methods may unwind. This restriction"},{"DocComment":" may be lifted in the future by ensuring unwinding out of an allocating function always"},{"DocComment":" aborts. If an implementor of `Allocator` also has drop glue or directly implements `Drop`,"},{"DocComment":" dropping the allocator must not result in an unwind."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" It is undefined behavior for the allocator to read, write, or deallocate any memory that"},{"DocComment":" is currently allocated. This memory is owned by the user; the allocator must not touch it."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Lastly, the methods on this trait must be *correct*; in particular, the layout requested"},{"DocComment":" must be respected, calls must zero out memory if the documentation so requires,"},{"DocComment":" returning an `AllocError` from a reallocating method must indeed ensure that"},{"DocComment":" the old pointer was not invalidated, and de/reallocating calls must accept layouts"},{"DocComment":" in the ranges defined by their documentation."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [*currently allocated*]: #currently-allocated-memory"},{"DocComment":" [*invalidated*]: #invalidating-memory-blocks"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null},"src":"Normal","generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self","variance":"Unknown"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"implied_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":12,"beg":{"line":201,"col":0},"end":{"line":466,"col":1}},"generated_from_span":null}},"origin":"WhereClauseOnTrait","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[1,0]}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}],"consts":[],"types":[],"methods":[{"params":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"variance":"Covariant","mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"name":"allocate","item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["alloc",0]},{"Ident":["Allocator",0]},{"Ident":["allocate",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":12,"beg":{"line":234,"col":4},"end":{"line":234,"col":76}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Attempts to allocate a block of memory."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" On success, returns a [`NonNull<[u8]>`][NonNull] meeting the size and alignment"},{"DocComment":" guarantees of `layout`. The returned block may have a larger size than specified"},{"DocComment":" by `layout.size()`, and may or may not have its contents initialized."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" It is recommended that overallocating as per the above is only performed if doing so"},{"DocComment":" is cheap; there is no guarantee that the caller is able to take advantage of the"},{"DocComment":" returned excess. Implementors are free to e.g. provide an alternate method to query"},{"DocComment":" available excess if doing so is expensive and should be left to the caller."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Note that the returned block of memory is considered [*currently allocated*]"},{"DocComment":" with this allocator (and equivalent allocators)."},{"DocComment":" Therefore, it is the responsibility of implementors of `Allocator` to make sure that"},{"DocComment":" this block of memory remains valid until it is [*invalidated*]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [*currently allocated*]: #currently-allocated-memory"},{"DocComment":" [*invalidated*]: #invalidating-memory-blocks"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Errors"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Returning `Err` indicates that either memory is exhausted or `layout` does not meet"},{"DocComment":" allocator's size or alignment constraints."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Implementations are encouraged to return `Err` on memory exhaustion rather than"},{"DocComment":" aborting, but this is not a strict requirement. (Specifically: it is *legal* to implement"},{"DocComment":" this trait atop an underlying native allocation library that aborts on memory exhaustion.)"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Clients wishing to abort computation in response to an allocation error are encouraged to"},{"DocComment":" call the [`handle_alloc_error`] function, rather than directly invoking `panic!` or similar."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`handle_alloc_error`]: ../../alloc/alloc/fn.handle_alloc_error.html"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Untagged":{"Ref":[{"Var":{"Bound":[0,0]}},{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[1,0]}}},"Shared"]}},{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":9,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}}],"output":{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":10,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":11,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Slice":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}},{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"Sized","parent_trait_refs":[{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"MetaSized","parent_trait_refs":[],"types":[],"vtable":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}],"types":[],"vtable":null}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}]}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}},{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":12,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"Sized","parent_trait_refs":[{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"MetaSized","parent_trait_refs":[],"types":[],"vtable":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":11,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Slice":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}},{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"Sized","parent_trait_refs":[{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"MetaSized","parent_trait_refs":[],"types":[],"vtable":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}],"types":[],"vtable":null}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}]}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":11,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Slice":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}},{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"Sized","parent_trait_refs":[{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"MetaSized","parent_trait_refs":[],"types":[],"vtable":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}],"types":[],"vtable":null}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}]}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}],"types":[],"vtable":null}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":11,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Slice":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}},{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"Sized","parent_trait_refs":[{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"MetaSized","parent_trait_refs":[],"types":[],"vtable":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}],"types":[],"vtable":null}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}]}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}},{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"Sized","parent_trait_refs":[{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"MetaSized","parent_trait_refs":[],"types":[],"vtable":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":12,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":12,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}],"types":[],"vtable":null}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":12,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}]},"builtin":null}}}},"default":null},"kind":{"TraitMethod":[2,0]}},null,{"params":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"variance":"Covariant","mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"name":"deallocate","item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["alloc",0]},{"Ident":["Allocator",0]},{"Ident":["deallocate",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":12,"beg":{"line":274,"col":4},"end":{"line":274,"col":66}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Deallocates the memory referenced by `ptr`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Safety"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" * `ptr` must denote a block of memory [*currently allocated*] via this allocator, and"},{"DocComment":" * `layout` must [*fit*] that block of memory."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Note that it is *immediate* language UB for a deallocation or reallocation to"},{"DocComment":" invalidate any outstanding references, smart pointers, etc.; thus, notably, an"},{"DocComment":" allocator that has been moved into its own [*currently allocated*] memory may"},{"DocComment":" not have its backing memory be freed, even if the allocator is never used again"},{"DocComment":" afterwards. This is due to the fact that such a deallocation would invalidate the"},{"DocComment":" `&self` reference passed to this method."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [*currently allocated*]: #currently-allocated-memory"},{"DocComment":" [*fit*]: #memory-fitting"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null},"signature":{"is_unsafe":true,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Untagged":{"Ref":[{"Var":{"Bound":[0,0]}},{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[1,0]}}},"Shared"]}},{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":11,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Scalar":{"Integer":{"Unsigned":"U8"}}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}},{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":9,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}}],"output":{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":"Tuple"}}}},"default":null},"kind":{"TraitMethod":[2,2]}},null,null,null],"vtable":{"id":8,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}},{"def_id":3,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["fmt",0]},{"Ident":["Display",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":14,"beg":{"line":1187,"col":0},"end":{"line":1187,"col":31}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Format trait for an empty format, `{}`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Implementing this trait for a type will automatically implement the"},{"DocComment":" [`ToString`][tostring] trait for the type, allowing the usage"},{"DocComment":" of the [`.to_string()`][tostring_function] method. Prefer implementing"},{"DocComment":" the `Display` trait for a type, rather than [`ToString`][tostring]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `Display` is similar to [`Debug`], but `Display` is for user-facing"},{"DocComment":" output, and so cannot be derived."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For more information on formatters, see [the module-level documentation][module]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [module]: ../../std/fmt/index.html"},{"DocComment":" [tostring]: ../../std/string/trait.ToString.html"},{"DocComment":" [tostring_function]: ../../std/string/trait.ToString.html#tymethod.to_string"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Completeness and parseability"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `Display` for a type might not necessarily be a lossless or complete representation of the type."},{"DocComment":" It may omit internal state, precision, or other information the type does not consider important"},{"DocComment":" for user-facing output, as determined by the type. As such, the output of `Display` might not be"},{"DocComment":" possible to parse, and even if it is, the result of parsing might not exactly match the original"},{"DocComment":" value."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" However, if a type has a lossless `Display` implementation whose output is meant to be"},{"DocComment":" conveniently machine-parseable and not just meant for human consumption, then the type may wish"},{"DocComment":" to accept the same format in `FromStr`, and document that usage. Having both `Display` and"},{"DocComment":" `FromStr` implementations where the result of `Display` cannot be parsed with `FromStr` may"},{"DocComment":" surprise users."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Internationalization"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Because a type can only have one `Display` implementation, it is often preferable"},{"DocComment":" to only implement `Display` when there is a single most \"obvious\" way that"},{"DocComment":" values can be formatted as text. This could mean formatting according to the"},{"DocComment":" \"invariant\" culture and \"undefined\" locale, or it could mean that the type"},{"DocComment":" display is designed for a specific culture/locale, such as developer logs."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If not all values have a justifiably canonical textual format or if you want"},{"DocComment":" to support alternative formats not covered by the standard set of possible"},{"DocComment":" [formatting traits], the most flexible approach is display adapters: methods"},{"DocComment":" like [`str::escape_default`] or [`Path::display`] which create a wrapper"},{"DocComment":" implementing `Display` to output the specific display format."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [formatting traits]: ../../std/fmt/index.html#formatting-traits"},{"DocComment":" [`Path::display`]: ../../std/path/struct.Path.html#method.display"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Implementing `Display` on a type:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::fmt;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" struct Point {"},{"DocComment":"     x: i32,"},{"DocComment":"     y: i32,"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" impl fmt::Display for Point {"},{"DocComment":"     fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {"},{"DocComment":"         write!(f, \"({}, {})\", self.x, self.y)"},{"DocComment":"     }"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let origin = Point { x: 0, y: 0 };"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(format!(\"The origin is: {origin}\"), \"The origin is: (0, 0)\");"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":"Display"},"src":"Normal","generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self","variance":"Unknown"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"implied_clauses":[],"consts":[],"types":[],"methods":[{"params":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"variance":"Covariant","mutability":"Unknown"},{"index":1,"name":null,"variance":"Covariant","mutability":"Unknown"},{"index":2,"name":null,"variance":"Invariant","mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"name":"fmt","item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["fmt",0]},{"Ident":["Display",0]},{"Ident":["fmt",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":14,"beg":{"line":1212,"col":4},"end":{"line":1212,"col":51}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":"Formats the value using the given formatter.\n\n# Errors\n\nThis function should return [`Err`] if, and only if, the provided [`Formatter`] returns [`Err`].\nString formatting is considered an infallible operation; this function only\nreturns a [`Result`] because writing to the underlying stream might fail and it must\nprovide a way to propagate the fact that an error has occurred back up the stack.\n"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::fmt;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" struct Position {"},{"DocComment":"     longitude: f32,"},{"DocComment":"     latitude: f32,"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" impl fmt::Display for Position {"},{"DocComment":"     fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {"},{"DocComment":"         write!(f, \"({}, {})\", self.longitude, self.latitude)"},{"DocComment":"     }"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!("},{"DocComment":"     \"(1.987, 2.983)\","},{"DocComment":"     format!(\"{}\", Position { longitude: 1.987, latitude: 2.983, }),"},{"DocComment":" );"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Untagged":{"Ref":[{"Var":{"Bound":[0,0]}},{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[1,0]}}},"Shared"]}},{"Untagged":{"Ref":[{"Var":{"Bound":[0,1]}},{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":14,"generics":{"regions":[{"Var":{"Bound":[0,2]}}],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}},"Mut"]}}],"output":{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":10,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":"Tuple"}}},{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":15,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"Sized","parent_trait_refs":[{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"MetaSized","parent_trait_refs":[],"types":[],"vtable":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":"Tuple"}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":"Tuple"}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}],"types":[],"vtable":null}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":"Tuple"}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}},{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"Sized","parent_trait_refs":[{"Untagged":{"kind":{"BuiltinOrAuto":{"builtin_data":"MetaSized","parent_trait_refs":[],"types":[],"vtable":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":15,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":15,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}],"types":[],"vtable":null}},"trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":15,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}}]},"builtin":null}}}},"default":null},"kind":{"TraitMethod":[3,0]}}],"vtable":{"id":13,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}},{"def_id":4,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["marker",0]},{"Ident":["Destruct",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":10,"beg":{"line":1063,"col":0},"end":{"line":1063,"col":38}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" A marker for types that can be dropped."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This should be used for `[const]` bounds,"},{"DocComment":" as non-const bounds will always hold for every type."}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":"Destruct","diagnostic_item":null},"src":"Normal","generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self","variance":"Unknown"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"implied_clauses":[],"consts":[],"types":[],"methods":[{"params":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"variance":"Covariant","mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"name":"drop_glue","item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["marker",0]},{"Ident":["Destruct",0]},{"Ident":["drop_glue",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":10,"beg":{"line":1063,"col":0},"end":{"line":1063,"col":38}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null},"signature":{"is_unsafe":true,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Untagged":{"Ref":[{"Var":{"Bound":[0,0]}},{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[1,0]}}},"Mut"]}}],"output":{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":"Tuple"}}}},"default":null},"kind":{"TraitMethod":[4,0]}}],"vtable":null},{"def_id":5,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["cmp",0]},{"Ident":["Eq",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":15,"beg":{"line":353,"col":0},"end":{"line":353,"col":58}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Trait for comparisons corresponding to [equivalence relations]("},{"DocComment":" https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equivalence_relation)."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The primary difference to [`PartialEq`] is the additional requirement for reflexivity. A type"},{"DocComment":" that implements [`PartialEq`] guarantees that for all `a`, `b` and `c`:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" - symmetric: `a == b` implies `b == a`"},{"DocComment":" - transitive: `a == b` and `b == c` implies `a == c`"},{"DocComment":" - consistent: `a != b` if and only if `!(a == b)`"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `Eq`, which builds on top of [`PartialEq`] also implies:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" - reflexive: `a == a`"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This property cannot be checked by the compiler, and therefore `Eq` is a trait without methods."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Violating this property is a logic error. The behavior resulting from a logic error is not"},{"DocComment":" specified, but users of the trait must ensure that such logic errors do *not* result in"},{"DocComment":" undefined behavior. This means that `unsafe` code **must not** rely on the correctness of these"},{"DocComment":" methods."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Floating point types such as [`f32`] and [`f64`] implement only [`PartialEq`] but *not* `Eq`"},{"DocComment":" because `NaN` != `NaN`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ## Derivable"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This trait can be used with `#[derive]`. When `derive`d, because `Eq` has no extra methods, it"},{"DocComment":" is only informing the compiler that this is an equivalence relation rather than a partial"},{"DocComment":" equivalence relation. Note that the `derive` strategy requires all fields are `Eq`, which isn't"},{"DocComment":" always desired."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ## How can I implement `Eq`?"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If you cannot use the `derive` strategy, specify that your type implements `Eq`, which has no"},{"DocComment":" extra methods:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" enum BookFormat {"},{"DocComment":"     Paperback,"},{"DocComment":"     Hardback,"},{"DocComment":"     Ebook,"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" struct Book {"},{"DocComment":"     isbn: i32,"},{"DocComment":"     format: BookFormat,"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" impl PartialEq for Book {"},{"DocComment":"     fn eq(&self, other: &Self) -> bool {"},{"DocComment":"         self.isbn == other.isbn"},{"DocComment":"     }"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" impl Eq for Book {}"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":"Eq"},"src":"Normal","generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self","variance":"Unknown"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"implied_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":15,"beg":{"line":353,"col":20},"end":{"line":353,"col":43}},"generated_from_span":null}},"origin":"WhereClauseOnTrait","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":9,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[1,0]}}},{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[1,0]}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}],"consts":[],"types":[],"methods":[null,null],"vtable":null},{"def_id":6,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["hash",0]},{"Ident":["Hash",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":16,"beg":{"line":185,"col":0},"end":{"line":185,"col":36}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" A hashable type."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Types implementing `Hash` are able to be [`hash`]ed with an instance of"},{"DocComment":" [`Hasher`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ## Implementing `Hash`"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" You can derive `Hash` with `#[derive(Hash)]` if all fields implement `Hash`."},{"DocComment":" The resulting hash will be the combination of the values from calling"},{"DocComment":" [`hash`] on each field."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" #[derive(Hash)]"},{"DocComment":" struct Rustacean {"},{"DocComment":"     name: String,"},{"DocComment":"     country: String,"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If you need more control over how a value is hashed, you can of course"},{"DocComment":" implement the `Hash` trait yourself:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::hash::{Hash, Hasher};"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" struct Person {"},{"DocComment":"     id: u32,"},{"DocComment":"     name: String,"},{"DocComment":"     phone: u64,"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" impl Hash for Person {"},{"DocComment":"     fn hash<H: Hasher>(&self, state: &mut H) {"},{"DocComment":"         self.id.hash(state);"},{"DocComment":"         self.phone.hash(state);"},{"DocComment":"     }"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ## `Hash` and `Eq`"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" When implementing both `Hash` and [`Eq`], it is important that the following"},{"DocComment":" property holds:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```text"},{"DocComment":" k1 == k2 -> hash(k1) == hash(k2)"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" In other words, if two keys are equal, their hashes must also be equal."},{"DocComment":" [`HashMap`] and [`HashSet`] both rely on this behavior."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Thankfully, you won't need to worry about upholding this property when"},{"DocComment":" deriving both [`Eq`] and `Hash` with `#[derive(PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Violating this property is a logic error. The behavior resulting from a logic error is not"},{"DocComment":" specified, but users of the trait must ensure that such logic errors do *not* result in"},{"DocComment":" undefined behavior. This means that `unsafe` code **must not** rely on the correctness of these"},{"DocComment":" methods."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ## Prefix collisions"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Implementations of `hash` should ensure that the data they"},{"DocComment":" pass to the `Hasher` are prefix-free. That is,"},{"DocComment":" values which are not equal should cause two different sequences of values to be written,"},{"DocComment":" and neither of the two sequences should be a prefix of the other."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For example, the standard implementation of [`Hash` for `&str`][impl] passes an extra"},{"DocComment":" `0xFF` byte to the `Hasher` so that the values `(\"ab\", \"c\")` and `(\"a\","},{"DocComment":" \"bc\")` hash differently."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ## Portability"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Due to differences in endianness and type sizes, data fed by `Hash` to a `Hasher`"},{"DocComment":" should not be considered portable across platforms. Additionally the data passed by most"},{"DocComment":" standard library types should not be considered stable between compiler versions."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This means tests shouldn't probe hard-coded hash values or data fed to a `Hasher` and"},{"DocComment":" instead should check consistency with `Eq`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Serialization formats intended to be portable between platforms or compiler versions should"},{"DocComment":" either avoid encoding hashes or only rely on `Hash` and `Hasher` implementations that"},{"DocComment":" provide additional guarantees."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`HashMap`]: ../../std/collections/struct.HashMap.html"},{"DocComment":" [`HashSet`]: ../../std/collections/struct.HashSet.html"},{"DocComment":" [`hash`]: Hash::hash"},{"DocComment":" [impl]: ../../std/primitive.str.html#impl-Hash-for-str"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":"Hash"},"src":"Normal","generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self","variance":"Unknown"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"implied_clauses":[],"consts":[],"types":[],"methods":[{"params":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"variance":"Covariant","mutability":"Unknown"},{"index":1,"name":null,"variance":"Covariant","mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"H","variance":"Invariant"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":16,"beg":{"line":198,"col":12},"end":{"line":198,"col":13}},"generated_from_span":null}},"origin":"WhereClauseOnFn","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[1,0]}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},{"clause_id":1,"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":16,"beg":{"line":198,"col":15},"end":{"line":198,"col":21}},"generated_from_span":null}},"origin":"WhereClauseOnFn","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":10,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[1,0]}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"name":"hash","item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["hash",0]},{"Ident":["Hash",0]},{"Ident":["hash",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":16,"beg":{"line":198,"col":4},"end":{"line":198,"col":45}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Feeds this value into the given [`Hasher`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::hash::{DefaultHasher, Hash, Hasher};"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut hasher = DefaultHasher::new();"},{"DocComment":" 7920.hash(&mut hasher);"},{"DocComment":" println!(\"Hash is {:x}!\", hasher.finish());"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Untagged":{"Ref":[{"Var":{"Bound":[0,0]}},{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[1,0]}}},"Shared"]}},{"Untagged":{"Ref":[{"Var":{"Bound":[0,1]}},{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[0,0]}}},"Mut"]}}],"output":{"Untagged":{"Adt":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":"Tuple"}}}},"default":null},"kind":{"TraitMethod":[6,0]}},null],"vtable":null},{"def_id":7,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["hash",0]},{"Ident":["BuildHasher",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":16,"beg":{"line":637,"col":0},"end":{"line":637,"col":21}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" A trait for creating instances of [`Hasher`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" A `BuildHasher` is typically used (e.g., by [`HashMap`]) to create"},{"DocComment":" [`Hasher`]s for each key such that they are hashed independently of one"},{"DocComment":" another, since [`Hasher`]s contain state."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For each instance of `BuildHasher`, the [`Hasher`]s created by"},{"DocComment":" [`build_hasher`] should be identical. That is, if the same stream of bytes"},{"DocComment":" is fed into each hasher, the same output will also be generated."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::hash::{BuildHasher, Hasher, RandomState};"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let s = RandomState::new();"},{"DocComment":" let mut hasher_1 = s.build_hasher();"},{"DocComment":" let mut hasher_2 = s.build_hasher();"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" hasher_1.write_u32(8128);"},{"DocComment":" hasher_2.write_u32(8128);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(hasher_1.finish(), hasher_2.finish());"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`build_hasher`]: BuildHasher::build_hasher"},{"DocComment":" [`HashMap`]: ../../std/collections/struct.HashMap.html"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":"BuildHasher"},"src":"Normal","generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self","variance":"Unknown"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"implied_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":16,"beg":{"line":637,"col":0},"end":{"line":704,"col":1}},"generated_from_span":null}},"origin":"WhereClauseOnTrait","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[1,0]}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},{"clause_id":1,"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":16,"beg":{"line":640,"col":4},"end":{"line":640,"col":24}},"generated_from_span":null}},"origin":{"TraitItem":0},"trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"TraitType":[{"Untagged":{"kind":"SelfId","trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":7,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[2,0]}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}},0,{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}]}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},{"clause_id":2,"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":16,"beg":{"line":640,"col":17},"end":{"line":640,"col":23}},"generated_from_span":null}},"origin":{"TraitItem":0},"trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":10,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"TraitType":[{"Untagged":{"kind":"SelfId","trait_decl_ref":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":7,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[2,0]}}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}},0,{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}]}}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}],"consts":[],"types":[{"params":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"name":"Hasher","attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Type of the hasher that will be created."}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":false},"default":null,"implied_clauses":[]},"kind":{"TraitType":[7,0]}}],"methods":[{"params":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"variance":"Covariant","mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"name":"build_hasher","item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["hash",0]},{"Ident":["BuildHasher",0]},{"Ident":["build_hasher",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":16,"beg":{"line":656,"col":4},"end":{"line":656,"col":43}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Creates a new hasher."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Each call to `build_hasher` on the same instance should produce identical"},{"DocComment":" [`Hasher`]s."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::hash::{BuildHasher, RandomState};"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let s = RandomState::new();"},{"DocComment":" let new_s = s.build_hasher();"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Untagged":{"Ref":[{"Var":{"Bound":[0,0]}},{"Untagged":{"TypeVar":{"Bound":[1,0]}}},"